t leaves for the remaining areas: 23.1m for 1000 CE, 24m for 1100 CE. The remaining area left covers 2,000,000 km2 and the polity of about 650,000 KM2 covered about 33% of this area. So, assuming an even distribution of population across the remaining landmass, a population magnitude estimate would be: 7.6m for 1000 CE, 7.9m for 1100 CE. According to maps of 800-900 CE there were about 6-7 other polities in the remaining region during the same time period.</i><br>'}], {'usage.total_tokens': 996, 'usage.prompt_tokens': 922})
